  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms will continue across the\nregion into tonight. HREF continues to show support for a few\nsevere storms during the afternoon and evening hours. Main\nconcerns continue to be large hail, damaging winds, heavy\nrainfall, and lightning. HREF updraft helicity and ensemble max\nwind gust tools also highlight the potential for a few severe\nstorms during the evening hours Wednesday.\n\nFor Thursday into the weekend, upper ridging will begin to\ndominate and build across the western U.S. with warmer and drier\nweather conditions. The ridge will slide downstream toward the\nweekend as high temperatures push well into the 90s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nTweaks were made for near term pops and winds mainly for\nconsistency and collaboration. Overall CAMS show decent support\non convective risk this evening and again Wednesday evening,\nthough confidence is below average on specific severe threat. The\nisolated coverage of stronger storms and exact track and evolution\nis somewhat uncertain- namely the northern extent of the risk \nthis evening. Confidence is growing on hot and dry weather \nunfolding for the weekend.",
